From e07d44594a58766e73b9acd0b7785317545ad2ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Weiye Chen <weiye.chen@rock-chips.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 15:17:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] backend: use gtkwaylandsink with synchronized transitions

Prefer gtkwaylandsink on native Wayland and use playbin3 with a
playbin fallback.

Keep the GTK top-level transparent and draw the preroll black background
inside BaconVideoWidget so GTK clips it to the current video allocation.
When returning to the browser, commit a top-level black overlay before
stopping the pipeline. Keep it until the browser page has painted so the
desktop is not exposed between parent and video subsurface updates.
